{"id":"angel-a-spirit","name":"Angel (A Spirit)","aliases":["Angel"],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:angel-a-spirit"],"groups":["A Celestial Spirit","Functions Of","Appearances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Angel","text":"A word signifying, both in the Hebrew and Greek, a “messenger,” and hence employed to denote any agent God sends forth to execute his purposes. It is used of an ordinary messenger (Job 1:14: 1 Sam. 11:3; Luke 7:24; 9:52), of prophets (Isa. 42:19; Hag. 1:13), of priests (Mal. 2:7), and ministers of the New Testament (Rev. 1:20). It is also applied to such impersonal agents as the pestilence (2 Sam. 24:16, 17; 2 Kings 19:35), the wind (Ps. 104:4). But its distinctive application is to certain heavenly intelligences whom God employs in carrying on his government of the world. The name does not denote their nature but their office as messengers. The appearances to Abraham at Mamre (Gen. 18:2, 22. Comp. 19:1), to Jacob at Peniel (Gen. 32:24, 30), to Joshua at Gilgal (Josh. 5:13, 15), of the Angel of the Lord, were doubtless manifestations of the Divine presence, “foreshadowings of the …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G32","lemma":"ἄγγελος","xlit":"ángelos","gloss":"compare G34 )","kjv":"angel, messenger","count":108,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H4397","lemma":"מֲלְאָךְ","xlit":"mălʼâk","gloss":"a messenger","kjv":"ambassador, angel, king, messenger","count":69,"share":0.17},{"strong":"G3772","lemma":"οὐρανός","xlit":"ouranós","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, heaven, sky","count":29,"share":0.07},{"strong":"G3173","lemma":"μέγας","xlit":"mégas","gloss":"","kjv":"exceedingly, great, high, large","count":22,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G2400","lemma":"ἰδού","xlit":"idoú","gloss":"used as imperative lo!","kjv":"--behold, lo, see","count":21,"share":0.05},{"strong":"G1799","lemma":"ἐνώπιον","xlit":"enṓpion","gloss":"in the face of","kjv":"before, in the presence  of, to","count":18,"share":0.04}],"verses":["Matt.1.20","Matt.1.24","Matt.2.13","Matt.2.